|> Exercise
    work=ing
    handle=_cosine_rule_geometric_4_

    Find expressions for
    areas A—F
    !! that allow you to find a formula for $c$ in terms of 
    !! all variables that do not contain “$c$” in their name:
    and use these to give a formula for $c$ in terms of
    $a$, $b$ and $\theta_{ab}$:

    |> Image
        src=tmp-images/_e5_cosine_rule_geometric_4_statement_v2.svg

    !! $$
    !! \begin{gathered}
    !! ab\cos\theta_{ab} \\
    !! bc\cos\theta_{bc} \\
    !! -ac\cos\theta_{ac} \\
    !! \end{gathered}
    !! $$

    |> Solution

        We can calculate each area as a plain “width $\times$ height”
        while keeping in mind that $\cos\theta_{ab} < 0$ (or more exactly
        that $\cos(2\eta - \theta_{ab}) = -\cos\theta_{ab}$),
        similarly to exercises >>_cosine_rule_geometric_1_,
        >>_cosine_rule_geometric_2_, and >>_cosine_rule_geometric_3_:
        !! the following
        !! figure is color-coded for equal areas:

        |> Image
            src=tmp-images/_e5_cosine_rule_geometric_4_sol1.svg

        I.e.,

        $$
        \begin{gathered}
        \te{A} = \te{F} = ab\cos\theta_{ab}\\
        \up{1.4}\te{B} = \te{E} = bc\cos\theta_{bc}\\
        \up{1.4}\te{C} = \te{D} = -ac\cos\theta_{ac}
        \end{gathered}
        $$

        from which...

        $$
        \Large c = \sqrt{c^2} = \sqrt{B - D} = \sqrt{E - C} = \sqrt{(b^2 - A) - (F - a^2)} = \sqrt{(b^2 - ab\cos\theta_{ab}) - (ab\cos\theta_{ab} - a^2)} = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\cos\theta_{ab}}
        $$

        ...where we use

        $$
        \begin{gathered}
        \te{B} = \te{E}\\
        \up{1.4}\te{D} = \te{C}
        \end{gathered}
        $$

        in the third equality, and

        $$
        \begin{gathered}
        \te{E} = b^2 - A\\
        \up{1.4}\te{D} = F - a^2
        \end{gathered}
        $$

        in the fourth equality. The answer is therefore...

        |> Boxed

            $$
            \Large c = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\cos\theta_{ab}}
            $$

        ...as in exercises >>_cosine_rule_geometric_1_, >>_cosine_rule_geometric_2_, and >>_cosine_rule_geometric_3_.
